          "overview": "## Webhound\n\nWebhound lets a person or agent set a dollar budget for a web investigation. The prompt defines the question; the budget defines how much effort Hound spends searching, reading, following leads, and verifying claims. A completed run can return a cited report or structured dataset, along with working documents, claim traces, sources, and an evidence pack. Hound is Webhound's research harness, built with DeepSeek V4 Pro and GPT-5.4; it is not a model selector.\n\nToolHive connects to Webhound through per-user OAuth with dynamic client registration and PKCE. Each user authorizes their own account; this entry contains no API key, bearer token, client secret, or shared publisher credential. Callers keep watching until Webhound reports `done=true` before treating a research run as finished.",
